# DeepSeek-V4-Pro split 4-way tensor parallel across 2 data-parallel ranks,
# against deepseek_v4_tp8dp1_speculative's TP8/DP1. Everything else is
# inherited, so the parallel layout is the entire difference between the two
# servers.
#
# Why this is worth measuring. The experts are 96.6% of the checkpoint (803 of
# 831 GiB) and EXPERT_PARALLEL shards them across all 8 GPUs either way, so TP
# only divides the 28 GiB of dense weight that is left. Halving TP therefore
# costs ~3.5 GiB per GPU -- and buys a second, independent KV pool, because DP
# ranks serve different requests while TP ranks replicate the same ones.
#
# That asymmetry is sharp here because V4 uses MLA, whose KV is one head however
# wide TP is (vLLM returns num_kv_heads=1 for MLA), so TP8 stores the same cache
# eight times. Estimated node-wide KV: ~18.9 GiB at TP8/DP1, ~30.8 GiB here.
#
# Estimated, not measured. Run it and read the pool off the serve log.

PROFILE_BASE=deepseek_v4_tp8dp1_speculative

TP_SIZE=4
DP_SIZE=2
